4→        return entries_for_interp, coords_for_interp\n   825→\n   826→    def _shape(self, t):\n   827→        first_dim_size = self.first_dim_size\n   828→        second_dim_size = self.second_dim_size\n   829→        t_size = len(t)\n   830→        return [first_dim_size, second_dim_size, t_size]\n   831→\n   832→\n   833→class ProcessedVariable2DSciKitFEM(ProcessedVariable2D):\n   834→    \"\"\"\n   835→    An object that can be evaluated at arbitrary (scalars or vectors) t and x, and\n   836→    returns the (interpolated) value of the base variable at that t and x.\n   837→\n   838→    Parameters\n   839→    ----------\n   840→    base_variables : list of :class:`pybamm.Symbol`\n   841→        A list of base variables with a method `evaluate(t,y)`, each entry of which\n   842→        returns the value of that variable for that particular sub-solution.\n   843→        A Solution can be comprised of sub-solutions which are the solutions of\n   844→        different models.\n   845→        Note that this can be any kind of node in the expression tree, not\n   846→        just a :class:`pybamm.Variable`.\n   847→        When evaluated, returns an array of size (m,n)\n   848→    base_variables_casadi : list of :class:`casadi.Function`\n   849→        A list of casadi functions. When evaluated, returns the same thing as\n   850→        `base_Variable.evaluate` (but more efficiently).\n   851→    solution : :class:`pybamm.Solution`\n   852→        The solution object to be used to create the processed variables\n   853→    \"\"\"\n   854→\n   855→    def __init__(\n   856→        self,\n   857→        base_variables,\n   858→        base_variables_casadi,\n   859→        solution,\n   860→        time_integral: Optional[pybamm.ProcessedVariableTimeIntegral] = None,\n   861→    ):\n   862→        self.dimensions = 2\n   863→        super().__init__(\n   864→            base_variables,\n   865→            base_variables_casadi,\n   866→            solution,\n   867→   