D. - For scikit-FEM 2D, guard with checks and return ProcessedVariable2DSciKitFEM when mesh is a ScikitSubMesh2D in the current collector. 2) Correct NumPy contiguous check - File: src/pybamm/solvers/processed_variable.py - Function: _is_f_contiguous - Replaced y.data.f_contiguous with y.flags.f_contiguous to use correct NumPy API. 3) xarray interpolation fill_value handling - File: src/pybamm/solvers/processed_variable.py - Method: ProcessedVariable._xr_interpolate - Wrapped xr.DataArray.interp with a try/except: - First try interp(..., kwargs={\"fill_value\": fill_value}) for newer xarray. - On TypeError (older xarray), do interp without kwargs then replace NaNs with fill_value if provided and not \"extrapolate\". 4) ProcessedVariable2DSciKitFEM super-init call - File: src/pybamm/solvers/processed_variable.py - Class: ProcessedVariable2DSciKitFEM - Initially changed to super().__init__, which caused failures because ProcessedVariable2D.__init__ assumes a secondary_mesh exists. - Final fix: explicitly call ProcessedVariable.__init__ to avoid the secondary_mesh-dependent assumptions in ProcessedVariable2D.__init__, which restores expected behavior for scikit-FEM variables that don\u2019t use secondary_mesh. New regression test added - File: tests/unit/test_solvers/test_processed_variable_meshless_postbuild_ext.py - Contents: - Construct a minimal model with a single variable y and IC y(0)=1. - After building the model but before solving, add three meshless variables: - \"t squared\": pybamm.t ** 2 - \"const\": pybamm.Scalar(3.14) - \"expr\": 2 * pybamm.t + pybamm.Scalar(1) - Solve with a ScipySolver on a short time grid. - Access sol[\"t squared\"].data, sol[\"const\"].data, sol[\"expr\"].data. - Assert correct shapes and values, and that interpolation calls return expected values. - This reproduces the user scenario and verifies no AttributeError is raised for meshless post-build variables. Test results - Ran the new regression test: - tests/unit/test_solvers/test_